  "text": "It sounds like you're caught between the need to rest and the weight of responsibility for your mom and the rest of your life. That guilt can be really heavy when you feel like every minute counts.\n\nSince you mentioned earlier that even small tasks feel monumental, perhaps framing rest as a \"small task\" could help shift your mindset? Instead of seeing it as abandoning your duties, could you try thinking of it as giving yourself permission to recharge so you can tackle those big tasks more effectively later?\n\nWould it help to set a very short, specific goal for yourself, like taking a 10-minute break or going for a short walk? Sometimes having a clear, manageable goal can make it feel less like \"stepping away\" and more like \"taking care of myself so I can come back stronger.\"",
